# `next dev` builds here instead of `.next`, so that a development build and a
# production build cannot overwrite each other (see ROOTLCO_DIST_DIR). It is a
# build directory like any other and must be ignored like one — CI never has it
# because CI never runs `next dev`, so only a developer ever sees the failure
# (P1-26-F-060).
